{#- Extractors:
  - response: AsIsExtractor()
-#}
<|SECTION:TASK|>
{% if tag -%}
You add new entries to one group on a page of a fantasy world's records: the "{{ tag }}" group of {{ page }}. The owner asked for: {{ prompt }}

Write what the owner asked for, as many as they asked for: one when they ask for one ("a guild", "an inn"), and never more than 3. Each new entry is tagged "{{ tag }}" and filed in {{ page }}. Each is a named thing with a proper name that fits the world, never a role, topic or practice without a name of its own. Keep each consistent with {{ page }} and the world, and never write again an entry the world already has (they are listed below).
{%- else -%}
You add new entries to a page of a fantasy world's records: {{ page }}. The owner asked for: {{ prompt }}

Write what the owner asked for, as many as they asked for: one when they ask for one ("a guild", "an inn"), and never more than 3. Each new entry is filed in {{ page }}, with its own tag saying what kind of entry it is ("guild", "custom", "river"). Each is a named thing with a proper name that fits the world, never a role, topic or practice without a name of its own. Keep each consistent with {{ page }} and the world, and never write again an entry the world already has (they are listed below).
{%- endif %}

{{ page }} ({{ page_kind }}{% if page_tag %}, {{ page_tag }}{% endif %}):
{% for text in page_facts -%}
- {{ text }}
{% endfor %}
{%- if tag %}
Already in its "{{ tag }}" group: {% if members %}{{ members | join("; ") }}{% else %}nothing yet{% endif %}.
{%- endif %}
{%- if filed %}
Also filed in {{ page }}: {{ filed | join("; ") }}.
{%- endif %}
{%- if nearby %}
Other entries near it: {{ nearby | join("; ") }}.
{%- endif %}

The world's calendar: it is now {{ now_label }}, year {{ now_year }}.
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
<|SECTION:FORMAT|>
Reply with only one JSON object, shaped exactly like this example:
{% if tag -%}
{"entries": [{"name": "...", "kind": "lore", "tag": "{{ tag }}", "line": "One claim saying what it is, in a full sentence."}]}
{%- else -%}
{"entries": [{"name": "...", "kind": "lore", "tag": "guild", "line": "One claim saying what it is, in a full sentence."}]}
{%- endif %}

- "name": the entry's proper name, in full.
- "kind": one of character, place, species, race, event, item, lore (a faith, order, guild, council, custom, law or field of knowledge is lore).
{%- if tag %}
- "tag": "{{ tag }}".
{%- else %}
- "tag": its own, a short word saying what kind of entry it is.
{%- endif %}
- "line": one sentence saying what it is and how it belongs in {{ page }}.

No commentary, no markdown fences, just the JSON object.
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{{ set_prepared_response('{') }}
